  "result": "The handover is implemented; typecheck is clean and the existing suite passes (617 tests). A throwaway smoke test of the main offer/accept/expiry/removal flow also passed and was deleted afterwards.\n\nTwo things behave differently from before, beyond the new API:\n\n- **Billing follows the recorded owner.** All billing operations now check the workspace's recorded owner from stored state, not the actor's role. A second member who merely holds the owner role can no longer manage billing (platform staff still can).\n- **Member role changes and removals use the stored role.** `updateMemberRole` and `removeMember` now authorise against the actor's current membership row when one exists, so an `Actor` built before a handover doesn't keep or lack rights by accident.\n\nNo visible test needed changing. I did not add server actions or UI for the handover, and the `scripts/manifest-parts` listings are not updated.",
